course: dictionary
lesson: 4593
title: Herbivores and what they eat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A herbivore is an animal that eats only plants, such as grass, leaves, fruit or seeds. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it. Here the sentence tells you what a herbivore eats.
explain: In a food chain, the arrows point from the food to the eater. «In a food chain such as grass, rabbit, fox, the grass is the producer, the rabbit a plant-eater or herbivore, and the fox a meat-eater or carnivore.» So the rabbit is the herbivore, and the grass is its food.
explain: Two other words sit beside herbivore. A carnivore eats meat, and an omnivore eats both plants and meat. «Herbivores eat plants, carnivores eat animals, and omnivores eat both.» Use this to sort any animal you meet.
explain: Teeth give clues too. «Teeth show what an animal eats: meat-eaters have sharp cutting teeth, plant-eaters flat grinding ones.» So herbivore teeth are flat, for grinding plants.
fact: A herbivore is an animal that eats only plants.
fact: Grass, leaves, fruit and seeds are all plant food for herbivores.
fact: Herbivores are usually primary consumers: they eat producers, which are plants.
fact: «Herbivore teeth» are often flat, for grinding plants.
fact: A carnivore eats meat, an omnivore eats both plants and meat, and a predator hunts other animals, which are its prey.
exercise: In the food chain grass, rabbit, fox, which animal is the herbivore? | *The rabbit | The grass is the herbivore | The fox and the rabbit | The fox
exercise: What is a herbivore? | A plant that eats insects | *An animal that eats only plants | An animal that eats only meat | A bird with long legs
exercise: «Bears and people are omnivores.» What does omnivore mean? | An animal that eats only plants | An animal that eats only meat | A plant that grows in the sea | *An animal that eats both plants and meat
test: Which teeth fit a herbivore? | Sharp cutting teeth for tearing meat | Long tusks for hunting | *Flat teeth for grinding plants | No teeth at all
test: A fox eats rabbits. Is the fox a herbivore? | Yes, all foxes are herbivores | *No, a fox is a carnivore, a meat-eater | Yes, because it lives in a field | No, because foxes are plants
exam: Which pair is correct? | A cow and a cat are both omnivores | A cow is a carnivore, and a cat is a herbivore | A cow is a producer, and a cat is a predator | *A cow is a herbivore, and a cat is a carnivore
